                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. анион бромоводородной кислоты Br⁻"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46c6f4f7-de28-3925-a781-c5075aee066f",
                        "entry_id": "f6973575-781d-3ec7-b9a4-2c7fff4aad3b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. бромсодержащее соединение, содержащее ковалентную связь бром-элемент"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "50c4a172-26a2-41f8-9f63-fd806b112775",
                                "sense_id": "46c6f4f7-de28-3925-a781-c5075aee066f",
                                "text": "Например: парааминофеноловые и метоловые проявители с поташем малочувствительны к воздействию бромида, глициновые и гидрохиноновые с едкой щёлочью, наоборот, чрезвычайно чувствительны."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d55189e-00e7-4e39-ac7f-7fb328d47051",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6973575-781d-3ec7-b9a4-2c7fff4aad3b",
                        "target_lang_word": "bromide",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bromide",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e89e087e-b11d-3658-9a77-64b903a2628f",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A binary compound of bromine and some other element or radical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3271fdb9-4c9d-3877-bbe0-95f8613e673f",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A binary compound of bromine and some other element or radical.",
                                            "Any salt of hydrobromic acid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd3baf47-a47c-3469-a7fa-58b181b379a5",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The anionic form of a bromine atom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ce412ae-cc2e-491a-994a-ae0a9415a4b7",
                                                "sense_id": "fd3baf47-a47c-3469-a7fa-58b181b379a5",
                                                "text": "“How fortunate Buddha, Mahomed, and Shakespeare were that their kind relations and doctors did not cure them of their ecstasy and their inspiration,” said Kovrin. “If Mahomed had taken bromide for his nerves, had worked only two hours out of the twenty-four, and had drunk milk, that remarkable man would have left no more trace after him than his dog. […]”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdd11a93-75ab-33a0-b72d-6a9bb174040f",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dull person with conventional thoughts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc624f89-71af-4952-bbb5-d1b47a5fb284",
                                                "sense_id": "bdd11a93-75ab-33a0-b72d-6a9bb174040f",
                                                "text": "My adviser at college was a bromide who had not had an original thought in years."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4972af5-271b-463a-9c2a-d55a4fa93feb",
                                                "sense_id": "bdd11a93-75ab-33a0-b72d-6a9bb174040f",
                                                "text": "The bromide conforms to everything sanctioned by the majority, and may be depended upon to be trite, banal, and arbitrary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57631353-b0d0-3fb6-9506-79319c67cc59",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A platitude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c057e51-b7be-4ae4-b01c-2aa3cc03174c",
                                                "sense_id": "57631353-b0d0-3fb6-9506-79319c67cc59",
                                                "text": "We hoped the speech would include reassurances, but instead it was merely one bromide after another."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e453c92-a77f-484d-b5d5-f8f830905fdf",
                                                "sense_id": "57631353-b0d0-3fb6-9506-79319c67cc59",
                                                "text": "No organicist metaphor, no irrelevant bromide that \"we are all part of one another,\" must be permitted to obscure this basic fact."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2756627f-0138-48ef-a5c3-7fd853e1359a",
                                                "sense_id": "57631353-b0d0-3fb6-9506-79319c67cc59",
                                                "text": "Gascoigne was annoyed by this. ‘Well, I wish you luck, Mr. Lauderback, in bringing Mr. Carver to justice,’ he said.\n‘Spare the bromide,’ Lauderback snapped. ‘Talk to me plain.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d47113f-8615-4d3c-9696-e741d918933c",
                                                "sense_id": "57631353-b0d0-3fb6-9506-79319c67cc59",
                                                "text": "Certainly not Facebook’s Mark Zuckerberg, who is clearly the Rupert Murdoch of his generation. He’s always justifying his cowardly choices with vacuous bromides about “free speech,” but he’s obviously just in it for the money — no matter how much his platform is used to destroy our democracy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0bdde3d3-a98c-36cd-94b1-71cc423ebab8",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dose of bromide taken as a sedative, or to reduce sexual appetite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8eef3e6d-7259-300c-8450-1e5020554631",
                                        "entry_id": "24b85a01-594a-3f16-a45a-27c1f2bbc669",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A print made on bromide paper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
